{
	title: 'Independent plugin directory activation and teardown',
	spec: 'The plugin loader supports multiple independently active directories through hookable activateDirectory and deactivateDirectory functions. Activating a directory loads sorted top-level TypeScript plugins and watches changes; repeated activation shares the pending or completed activation. Deactivation stops its watcher, removes only its loaded files and hooks, invokes cleanup, cancels pending imports and scans, and permits later reactivation. Closing the loader deactivates every directory and invalidates direct pending loads. A watcher or old activation must never resurrect a deactivated directory or tear down a newer activation. Hook ordering remains filename-first with full path breaking same-name ties so multiple directories have stable composition independent of activation order. Existing Hal-home startup and reviewed portable sync remain unchanged; extra directories do not enter the home history or sync namespace. The lifecycle functions are plugin hook points, not an enforced sandbox. Project discovery and session reference counting are a separate trust-gated integration: user decision is to deactivate when the last open session leaves a project. No automatic project imports before that gate exists. Preserve permanent regression coverage for async cancellation and ownership across directories.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Restored invariant: directory teardown and loader close invalidate pending registrations, including imports not yet present in the loaded-file map. An activation identity guards its scan and watcher; deactivation deletes pending generations, closes its watcher and releases per-directory entries. Full-path hook ownership gives deterministic basename ties. Top-level module evaluation itself cannot be canceled, so operational work belongs in setup and cleanup. Directory functions do not count sessions; task tzr integrates trusted discovery and last-session lifetimes. One watcher per active directory, no new polling; unload scans current loaded/pending paths and releases its state. Existing sync still follows only the home directory. Verified ./test: 1690 pass, 2 skip, 0 fail, plus full TypeScript and lint; focused plugin/sync/history/report tests: 39 pass. After simplifying the race fixture, all 20 loader tests passed again. No project directories are auto-loaded by this change.'
	],
